do you think i should have told them  potterheads get ready to discover some  of the darkest  best kept secrets about the harry potter  world jk rowling and the cast have made  some jaw-dropping revelations since the  series came to an end but many have  remained well hidden  so we're using our very best lumos spell  to shine a light on all the most  fascinating little-known details  i'm ready ask me any question dan  radcliffe  interviewed jk rowling for a special  feature on the deathly hallows part 2  dvd  and the author said that the original  plan was for the main trio to survive  but then midway through the series which  reflects she wasn't in a happy place at  the time  she started thinking she might polish  one of them off out of sheer spite  and it would have been wrong but in her  absolute heart of hearts she couldn't  just imagine the fan backlash if she'd  gone through with it and you don't know  how it feels  just imagine if we'd ended up with a  different actor playing ron  halfway through the series it seems  impossible but rupert grant admitted in  an interview with the independent that  he almost quit after goblet of fire  he explained that he just finished his  gcse exams  and thought to himself do i actually  want to keep doing this  it's a bit of a drag he considered it a  big sacrifice losing his anonymity and  not being able to do normal stuff  the actor described life as a little bit  scary at that point  thank goodness he didn't go through with  thinking he was done there's  only one ron weasley who do you imagine  wants to attack  children like yourself dolores umbridge  is one of the characters jk rowling  feels  purest dislike for but that doesn't mean  she didn't create a fascinating  backstory for her  on pottermore rowling revealed that  despite claiming to be a pureblood  umbridge actually had a muggle mother  and her brother was a squib  umbridge despised her father for his  lack of ambition  however when she was 15 dolores remained  with her dad when the family split as  they both blamed her mom for her  brother's lack of magical ability  does that information make you view  umbrage in a new light  i really hate children we were relieved  that arthur weasley survived nagini's  attack at the ministry of magic in the  order of the phoenix but jk rowling had  planned for that to be the end of him  she revealed to the today show that he  got a reprieve because she couldn't bear  to part with him as there are very few  good fathers in the book the author  believes you could make a case for  arthur being the only good father in the  whole series  but his survival was at lupin's cost  without whom  i would not be here as jk rowling  changed her mind about mr weasley she  felt she had to do away with a different  father and that was poor remus lupin  can you imagine what this series would  have been like if lupine had survived  but arthur hadn't  the author didn't take lupin and tonks's  fate lightly in 2016 she tweeted that  because arthur lived  lupin had to take his place she added  i'm sorry i didn't enjoy doing it  the only time my editor ever saw me cry  was over the fate of teddy  i wouldn't be standing here without him  jk rowling did away with lots of parents  in her books but she clearly feels a  sense of responsibility for the orphan  she created in an interview with the  today show the author revealed that she  wrote the 19 years later epilogue to  show that the world was a better place  and there was new life  and that was particularly for teddy  lupin's sake he was in that epilogue  kissing bill and fleur weasley's eldest  daughter victoire  at king's cross station rowling wanted  to show the readers that he was okay and  must be quite happy  there is a plot to make most terrible  things happen  of all the tragic ends that jk rowling  wrote dobby's fate  upset many fans i didn't mean to offend  you or anything  but guess what the author actually said  sorry to fans for what she did to the  wonderful house elf  just like she did about lupin rowling  has stood by most of her character's  endings despite fan reaction  but on the anniversary of the battle of  hogwarts in 2018  she took to twitter to apologize for  dobby's demise if only she'd had a  change of heart before the book had been  published  dobby feels most aggrieved sir the harry  potter universe included gothic  creatures like werewolves but never a  vampire teacher  however that very nearly did happen in  an article on pottermore in december  2014  jk rowling revealed that she toyed with  the idea of a vampire teacher called  trokar  but that got edited out rowling put paid  to fan chatter about snape being a  vampire too  even though he has an unhealthy pallor  and is sometimes described as looking  like a huge bat  in an interview with rte in 2011 alan  rickman revealed that jk rowling had  given him one little piece of  information  about how to play snape and he never  shared it with anyone  after he passed away rowling shared it  on twitter in january 2016  i told alan what lies behind the word  always of course she's referring to the  moment dumbledore asks snape if he's  still in love with lily  and snape replies always so rickman knew  what was motivating his character  all along come on tom let's finish this  the way we started  harry and voldemort were connected  through the horcruxes but did you also  know they were connected through their  family trees  wait what jk rowling revealed this  fascinating piece of info when she gave  us an insight into the potter family  harry's dad james inherited the  invisibility cloak from his ancestor  ignatus preverel and tom riddle was also  related to the previous family that's  why he had the resurrection stone  although there are hints in the deathly  hallows it wasn't made  explicit that's who we really are  of course authors often take inspiration  from people they've met  and jk rowling is no different in a  pottermore article she revealed that she  based dolores umbridge on a couple of  people  one was her teacher who loved twee  accessories including little plastic bow  slides  she wore sickly sweet and girlish  clothes with frills  and carried undersized handbags as for  the kitten pictures that was inspired by  a bigoted spiteful woman rowling shared  an office with  the author noted that a love of all  things saccharin often seems present  where there is a lack of real warmth or  charity  imagine being one of those women and  discovering you were part of the  inspiration for such an unpleasant  character  you know deep down  you deserve to be punished if you  thought rita skeeter would have changed  her ways  think again on the pottermore site jk  rowling wrote a report on the quidditch  world cup in 2014  in character as rita and the gossip  columnist was still making nasty jibes  at harry ron and hermione  commenting on their aging hair she also  kept up her habit for unpleasant  speculation  noticing a cut on harry's face rita  wondered if ginny had cursed him and if  there were problems in their marriage  typical you two may even make the front  page  there are so many major characters jk  rowling disposed of without regret but  guess what  she felt bad about the end she wrote for  a very minor character  florian fortescue the owner of the ice  cream parlor on diagon alley who was  dragged away by voldemort's servants  in the half blood prince go figure on  pottermore rowling revealed that  although fortescue wasn't the first  wizard voldemort disposed of for knowing  too much he was the only one she felt  guilty about because it was all her  fault  fortescue was going to be the conduit  for clues to help harry search for the  deathly hallows but rowling then decided  phineas nicholas black was a much more  satisfactory option  he must not be seen if you thought  dumbledore always looked like he could  see harry when he was under the  invisibility cloak you're right  jk rowling revealed in a web chat on the  bloomsbury site that dumbledore could  perform  magic without needing to say the  incantation out loud and what spell was  it that he used  hominem revellio hermione used the human  presence revealing spell in the deathly  hallows  in a deleted scene from deathly hallows  part 1 we finally get to see aunt  petunia in a more human light  or at least we would have done had it  not been cut as harry is saying his  final farewells to the dursleys he has  an exchange with his mom's sister that  reveals she didn't entirely dislike lily  yes petunia was envious and unkind but  she also kept loving lily deep down  had this scene made the final cut it  would have given us a different view on  the character  i lost the sister  which of these secrets changes the way  you view the harry potter series the  most  we want to know what you think but as we  aren't magical enough to read minds  you'll have to tell us in the comments  section instead  thanks for watching

